Description: Let the power plugin's sounds follow the system sounds setting.
 The power plugin plays sounds when the power cable goes in and out, when the lid is opened and
 closed, and when a battery runs low, and it hands all of them to libcanberra directly. libcanberra
 applies the desktop's system sounds setting, org.gnome.desktop.sound event-sounds, only in its GTK
 wrappers, so these sounds play even with System Sounds switched off in Settings, and nothing
 switches them off.
 .
 The setting is read in the plugin instead, around the plays only, so the low battery notification
 still appears, without its sound, and the lid still suspends. The critical battery sounds are left
 alone, since they are the last warning before the machine puts itself away. With the sounds off the
 canberra context is not created for these events either, so the plugin stops connecting to the
 sound server for them.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
--- a/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
+++ b/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
@@ -781,6 +781,19 @@
         }
 };
 
+/* The sounds of this plugin reach libcanberra directly, and libcanberra applies the desktop's
+ * system sounds setting only in its GTK wrappers, so the setting is read here instead. The sounds
+ * for the power cable, for the lid and for a low battery follow it. The critical battery sounds do
+ * not, since they are the last warning before the machine puts itself away.
+ */
+static gboolean
+event_sounds_enabled (void)
+{
+        g_autoptr(GSettings) settings = g_settings_new ("org.gnome.desktop.sound");
+
+        return g_settings_get_boolean (settings, "event-sounds");
+}
